[{:adr/authoritative_for ["dossier.lei-site-archive real client" "cloud-itonami-lei-* archive data connected into the dossier enrichment layer"], :adr/topic "isic-8291-lei-site-archive-enrichment", :adr/related ["adr-2607182500" "adr-2607182400" "adr-2607110300"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607182600-isic-8291-lei-site-archive-enrichment", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-18", :adr/body "# ADR-2607182600: cloud-itonami-isic-8291 dossier -- connect cloud-itonami-lei-* archive data into the enrichment layer\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-18\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (owner directive: \\\"do it\\\", following the closing suggestion of ADR-2607182500 to connect its new site.journal.edn data into the dossier enrichment layer, same tier as Common Crawl)\n**Scope**: `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-8291` (child commit `3efaeaec9af8`), west pin advance.\n\n## Decision\n\nAdded `dossier.lei-site-archive` (keyless, JVM-only `.clj`): reads this workspace's own 109 `cloud-itonami-lei-<LEI>` archive repos' `80-data/public/site.journal.edn` (ADR-2607182500) as a SECOND non-authoritative web-presence enrichment source, at the exact same governed-vs-enrichment tier `dossier.commoncrawl` (ADR-2607182400) established: no `->company` mapper, not added to `dossier.facts`'s catalog, not wired into `dossier.live-store`'s decorator chain -- our own periodic site check is real, but it is not a registry fact any more than a Common Crawl hit is. `->enrichment` returns the exact same shape `dossier.commoncrawl/->enrichment` does, so a caller can use either source interchangeably.\n\nAccepts either a bare LEI or a dossier-canonical `lei-<LEI>` id (the same shape `dossier.gleif/->company`'s `:id` already produces), normalizing case and the repo-naming convention (lowercase LEI in the repo name, uppercase LEI as the stored value) internally.\n\n## Why this is a genuinely complementary source, not a duplicate of Common Crawl\n\n`dossier.commoncrawl` is a live lookup against a general-purpose crawl that may not have indexed any given site. `dossier.lei-site-archive` reads OUR OWN already-fetched, LEI-keyed archive -- for the 109 companies it covers, coverage is real and dense (106/109 successfully checked, ADR-2607182500) at the cost of only covering companies this workspace has already registered an archive repo for.\n\n## Verification\n\nLive-verified against the REAL archived data (not just offline fixtures) -- fetched from `raw.githubusercontent.com/cloud-itonami/...` for real:\n\n- Wabtec, both input forms (bare LEI `06BTX5UWZD0GQ5N5Y745` and dossier-canonical `lei-06btx5uwzd0gq5n5y745`) -- both correctly resolved the same real enrichment record.\n- The known nasdaq.com failure case (ADR-2607182500's `:site/http-status 0` record) -- correctly reports `has-web-presence? false`, no fabricated title/description.\n- A nonexistent LEI -- correctly `nil` (distinct from a checked-but-failed `false`).\n- `fetch-blueprint` -- correctly parsed the real company-identity record.\n\nOffline test suite (fixture-based, same discipline as `dossier.commoncrawl-test`) covers the same cases plus id-normalization and the \\\"pick the LATEST re-check, not the first\\\" folding logic. Full actor suite: 133/529 assertions green (was 123/510), clj-kondo clean.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- The dossier actor's non-authoritative enrichment tier now has two real, complementary sources (Common Crawl for anything on the open web; this workspace's own LEI archive for the 109 companies it already tracks), both returning the same shape, neither ever masquerading as a registry fact.\n- Follow-up (not done here): a small composition helper trying `lei-site-archive` first and falling back to `dossier.commoncrawl` would be a natural next step if a caller wants \\\"best available enrichment\\\" without picking a source explicitly -- left as a documented option, not built speculatively.\n", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/date "2026-07-18", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607182600: cloud-itonami-isic-8291 dossier -- connect cloud-itonami-lei-* archive data into the enrichment layer", :adr/source-format "edn"}]